  "note": "Triennial election of the Portstewart Urban District Council, poll fixed for Wednesday 21 May 1952. Thirteen nominations were lodged for the twelve seats; Mr. T. F. B. Johnston withdrew the next day, leaving twelve candidates for twelve seats, so there was no election and the twelve were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 8 May 1952, p. 6; Derry Journal, 9 May 1952, p. 6). Johnston's withdrawal left exactly twelve candidates for the twelve seats, so the twelve were returned unopposed. Citation unconfirmed: the names were not all found on the cited page (verification 5 Nov 2026). Returned unopposed."
